nown as the Namibian War of Independence, and sometimes denoted in South Africa as the Angolan Bush War, was a largely asymmetric conflict that occurred in Namibia (then South West Africa), Zambia, and Angola from 26 August 1966 to 21 March 1990. It was fought between the South African Defence Force (SADF) and the People's Liberation Army of Namibia (PLAN), an armed wing of the South West African People's Organisation (SWAPO). Outcome: Military stalemate; Angolan Tripartite Accord, leading to:; Withdrawal of South African forces from Namibia; withdrawal of Cuban forces from Angola; 1989 Namibian parliamentary elections; SWAPO government assuming power in Namibia. Cost: Dead: Namibian civilians dead: 947–1,087.","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1993848"],["Journal for Studies in Humanities and Social Sciences","https://repository.unam.edu.na/bitstream/handle/11070/732/waking%20the%20deadocr.pdf?sequence=1"],["britannica.com","http://www.britannica.com/EBchecked/topic/402283/Namibia/44019/The-road-to-Namibia"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_African_Border_War"]]},{"c":5,"k":0,"t":"Battle of Mongua","w":"17 August 1915 – 20 August 1915","y":1915,"p":"Môngua","s":"1915 battle","o":"Southern Angola campaign","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2889355"]],"u":11},{"c":5,"k":0,"t":"Battle of Otavi","w":"1 July 1915","y":1915,"p":"Otavi","s":"battle in 1915 during the First World War","o":"South-West Africa campaign","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2896257"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Otavi"]],"u":13},{"c":5,"k":0,"t":"Battle of Trekkopjes","w":"26 April 1915","y":1915,"p":"Trekkopje","s":"1915 battle","o":"South-West Africa campaign","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3636641"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Trekkopjes"]],"u":13},{"c":5,"k":5,"t":"Southern Angola campaign","w":"July 1915 – 4 September 1915","y":1915,"p":"Ovamboland","s":"1915 mil